// A meter, conditions, a hook and an ending working together: the night chill.
//
// The meter keeps a number (player.cold) that drops by itself each turn and has
// stages; each stage is a condition with effects that last while it is active.

== meter cold
name: Cold
value: player.cold
// One point wears off every turn.
decay: 1
limit: 10
stages:
    3: chilled
    6: shivering
// At the limit the game ends: "~ ending <id>" ends the game and the epilogue
// (rules/endings.fsc) plays. Days are warm enough that a single night outdoors
// rarely gets this far.
at limit:
    The cold settles into your bones, and you curl up under the pines for good.
    ~ ending frozen_in_the_woods

== condition chilled
name: Chilled
shows: Dex -1.
while active:
    player.dexterity - 1
enters:
    **You're getting cold.** A warm drink or a coat would help.
still:
    You're still chilled.

== condition shivering
name: Shivering
shows: Dex -2, Str -1.
while active:
    player.dexterity - 2
    player.strength - 1
enters:
    **You're shivering hard.** Get indoors before the night gets worse.
still:
    You can't stop shivering.

// A condition with a duration, given by an item: "~ condition warmed_up for 6 hours".
== condition warmed_up
name: Warmed up
shows: The tea keeps you warm.
while active:
    player.stamina + 1
ends:
    The warmth of the tea fades.

// A hook runs at a moment in time; "each turn" is every three-hour turn.
// `when:` is checked each time. Here: outdoors at night, the cold creeps in,
// unless the player wears the wool coat or is warmed up.
== hook night_chill
on: each turn
when: time is night and not player is in cabin and not player wears wool_coat and not player has condition warmed_up
do:
    ~ meter cold + 2
